{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Hasten:</b> For almost my spirit has failed, and I am likened to those who go down into the pit. The meaning is twofold: either [it connects to] the word 'do not hide,' on account of something else, as in 'before the mountains were born' and 'let me not be likened to those who go down into the pit.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 143, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:36.158972191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}